{"schema_version":1,"source_commit":"100560de6c9f68c2875097d40a2012a84c784179","scope":"Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam Canto 2, Chapter 5 — Śrīdhara Svāmī word-for-word gloss","source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","entries":[{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":1,"end":1,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["पञ्चमे","in the fifth [canto]"],["नारदेन पृष्टः","questioned by Nārada"],["सृष्ट्य्-आदि वक्ता अजः","Brahmā, who speaks about creation and the rest"],["हरेर् लीलाम्","the pastimes of Hari"],["विराट्-सृष्टिम्","the creation of the universal form"],["काल-कर्मादि-शक्तिभिः","through the powers of time, action and the rest"],["नारद-प्रश्नम् आह","he states Nārada's question"],["भूत-भावन","O creator of beings"],["सर्वेषां पूर्वज अनादे","O beginningless one, the forefather of all"],["ज्ञानं तत्-साधनम्","knowledge, and its means"],["तद् विजानीहि विशेषेण ज्ञापय","know it; explain it distinctly"],["आत्म-तत्त्वं नितरां दृश्यते येन","by which the truth of the Self is clearly seen"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":2,"end":2,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["उपलक्षण-भूतं विश्वम्","the universe, which serves as an indication"],["आत्म-ज्ञान-साधनम्","a means of knowledge of the Self"],["यद् रूपं येन रूप्यते प्रकाश्यते","the form by which something is formed or made manifest"],["यद् अधिष्ठानम् यद् आश्रयम्","that which is the substratum, that which is the support"],["यतो येन सृष्टम्","from whom, by whom it is created"],["यत् संस्थं यस्मिन् लीयते","that in which it rests, in which it dissolves"],["यत् परं यद् अधीनम्","that which is supreme, that upon which it depends"],["यच् च यद् आत्मकम्","and that of which it consists"],["स्वतः सत्-कारणतः वा","whether it is real in itself or through its cause"],["तस्य तत्त्वं याथार्थ्यम्","its truth, its reality"],["तत्त्वतः वद","tell it truly"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":3,"end":3,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["न जानामि इति न वक्तव्यम्","one should not say ‘I do not know’"],["भूतं जातम्","what has come into being"],["भव्यं जनिष्यमाणम्","what will come into being"],["भवत् जायमानम्","what is coming into being"],["तेषां प्रभुः","the Lord of them"],["विशिष्टेन ज्ञानेन अवसितम् निश्चितम्","determined through special knowledge"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":4,"end":4,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["आस्ताम् इदम्","let this matter be"],["आदौ तावत् त्वाम् एव कथय","first, speak about yourself"],["यतो विज्ञानं यस्य","from whom knowledge arises"],["विज्ञान-दः","the giver of knowledge"],["यद्-आधारः यद्-आश्रयः","whose foundation, whose support"],["यत्-परः यद्-अधीनः","whose supreme, whose dependent"],["यद्-आत्मकः यत्-स्वरूपः","whose essence, whose nature"],["त्वम् एव स्वतन्त्रः परमेश्वरः","you alone are the independent Supreme Lord"],["एकोऽसहायः","one, without a second"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":5,"end":5,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["आत्मनि भावयसे","you bring forth and maintain within yourself"],["पालयसि","you protect"],["स्वयम् एव","by yourself alone"],["पराभवम् अप्रापयन्","not allowing defeat or harm"],["अक्लमः श्रम-रहितः","without fatigue, free from effort"],["ऊर्णनाभिः","a spider"],["आत्मन एव शक्तिम् अवष्टभ्य","drawing upon its own power"],["सृजति तद्वत्","it creates; in the same way"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":6,"end":6,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तस्माद् अहम्","therefore I"],["अस्मिन् विश्वस्मिन्","in this universe"],["परम् उत्तमम्","the superior and highest"],["अपरम् अधमम्","the inferior and lower"],["समं मध्यमं च","and the equal and middle"],["मनुष्यादि-रूपम्","forms such as human"],["द्विपदत्वादि-गुणः","qualities such as being two-footed"],["शुक्लत्वादिः","whiteness and the like"],["सद्-असत्-स्थूलं सूक्ष्मं च","existent or non-existent, gross or subtle"],["त्वत्त एव सर्वं भवति","everything arises from you alone"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":7,"end":7,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तथा-विधोऽपि","although you are of such a nature"],["भवान् तपः अचरत्","you performed austerity"],["तेन नोऽस्मान् खेदयसे","by that you trouble us"],["मोहयसि","you bewilder"],["परा-शङ्काम्","a serious doubt"],["ईश्वर-अन्तर-आशङ्काम्","the suspicion of another Lord"],["प्रयच्छसि","you give rise to"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["यथा अहम् त्वया अनुशासितः","just as I have been instructed by you"],["शिक्षितः सन्","having been taught"],["बुध्ये बुध्येयम्","I understand, may I understand"],["तथा विजानीहि","explain it in that way"],["विशेषेण ज्ञापय","make it especially clear"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":9,"end":9,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["वत्स हे पुत्र","O dear child, O son"],["तव इदं विचिकित्सितम्","this doubt of yours"],["सन्देहः तत्-पूर्वकः प्रश्नः","a question preceded by uncertainty"],["सम्यक्","properly, well"],["कारुणिकस्य तव","of you, who are compassionate"],["पर-धर्म-प्रदर्शने","in explaining the dharma of others"],["भगवद्-वीर्य-प्रकाशने","in revealing the power of Bhagavān"],["प्रवर्तितः अस्मि","I have been engaged"],["त्वं जिज्ञासुः","you, though desiring to know"],["मयि कृपाम् एव कृतवान्","have shown compassion toward me"]],"note":"The source runs “प्रदर्शनेभगवद्-वीर्य”; the WFW separates the two compounds at the evident phrase boundary and records the source spacing defect."},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":10,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["ननु त्वम् एव भगवान्","surely you yourself are Bhagavān"],["एकः सृजसि भूतानि","‘you alone create beings’"],["सत्यम्","it is true"],["माम् ईश्वरत्वेन प्रभाषसे","you describe me as the Lord"],["न अत्यन्तम् अनृतम्","not entirely untrue"],["एतावत्-प्रभावस्य","of this much power"],["मत्तः परम् ईश्वरम् अविज्ञाय","not knowing the Lord who is beyond me"],["सादृश्यात् भ्रान्तिः","the mistake arises from resemblance"],["न तु बुद्धि-पूर्वम् अनृतम्","it is not a deliberate falsehood"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":11,"end":11,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तर्हि कः असौ ईश्वरः","then who is that Lord?"],["भक्त्या नमस्कुर्वन्","bowing with devotion"],["येन स्व-प्रकाशेन","by whose self-luminosity"],["रोचितं प्रकाशितम्","what is made bright, manifested"],["सृष्ट्या अभिव्यक्तं करोमि","I make it manifest through creation"],["अर्कादयः","the sun and the other luminaries"],["तत्-प्रकाश्यम् एव प्रकाशयन्ति","they illuminate only what is illumined by him"],["तस्य भासा सर्वम् इदं विभाति","by his light all this shines"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":12,"end":12,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तस्मै नमः","obeisance to him"],["धीमहि","we meditate"],["यस्य मायया विमोहिताः","deluded by whose māyā"],["युष्मद्-आदयः","you and others"],["मां जगद्-गुरुम्","me, the teacher of the universe"],["जगत्-कारणम् वदन्ति","they call the cause of the universe"],["मनसा नमनं कुर्वीमहि","may we bow with the mind"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":13,"end":13,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["माया-सम्बन्ध-उक्तेः","from the statement that he is related to māyā"],["तस्या दुर्जयत्व-उक्तेः","and from the statement that it is hard to overcome"],["परमेश्वरस्य अपि","even for the Supreme Lord"],["मत्-कपटम् असौ जानाति","she knows my deceit"],["दृष्टि-पथे स्थातुम्","to stand in his field of vision"],["विलज्जमानया","being ashamed"],["स्व-कार्यम् अकुर्वत्या","not performing her own work"],["मायया विमोहिताः","deluded by māyā"],["दुर्धियः अविद्या-वृत-ज्ञानाः","foolish, their knowledge covered by ignorance"],["विकत्थन्ते श्लाघन्ते","they boast"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":14,"end":14,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["स्वस्माद् अन्यम् परमेश्वरम्","a Supreme Lord other than himself"],["यद्-अधिष्ठानम् इत्य्-आदि-नव-प्रश्नानाम्","of the nine questions beginning ‘the substratum’"],["द्रव्यम् महा-भूतानि","substance means the great elements"],["उपादान-रूपाणि","which are the material cause"],["कर्म जन्म-निमित्तम्","action is the cause of birth"],["कालः तत्-क्षोभकः","time agitates them"],["स्वभावः तत्-परिणाम-हेतुः","nature is the cause of their transformation"],["जीवः भोक्ता","the living being is the enjoyer"],["वासुदेवात् परः अन्योऽर्थो नास्ति","there is no other reality beyond Vāsudeva"],["कारण-अव्यतिरेकात् कार्यस्य","because the effect is not separate from its cause"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":15,"end":15,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["नारायणः परः कारणम्","Nārāyaṇa is the supreme cause"],["शास्त्र-योनि-प्रतिपादनेन","by showing that scripture is the source"],["ईश्वरे प्रमाणम्","there is proof of the Lord"],["सर्व-ज्ञत्वादिकम्","his omniscience and the rest"],["देवाः तद्-अङ्गाज् जाताः","the gods were born from his limbs"],["न तद्-व्यतिरिक्ताः","they are not separate from him"],["लोकाः स्वर्गादयः","the worlds, beginning with heaven"],["तद्-आनन्दांशाः","are portions of his bliss"],["मखाः तत्-साधन-भूताः","sacrifices are means to that"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":16,"end":16,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["योगः प्राणायामादिः","yoga means breath control and the like"],["तपः तत्-साध्यं चित्त-एकाग्र्यम्","austerity is concentration of mind, achieved through it"],["ज्ञानं तत्-साध्यम्","knowledge is its result"],["गतिः तत्-फलम्","the destination is its fruit"],["सर्वं तद्-अधीनम्","everything depends on him"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":17,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तर्हि त्वं किं करोषि","then what do you do?"],["तस्य सृज्यम् अपि","although it is his creation"],["तेन सृष्टः अहम् सृजामि","created by him, I create"],["ईक्षया कटाक्षेण","by his glance"],["द्रष्टुः इत्य्-आदयः","the reasons beginning with ‘the seer’"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["जीव-ईश्वर-विभाग-हेतुम्","the cause of the distinction between the living being and the Lord"],["निर्गुणस्य अपि ईश्वरस्य","even of the Lord, who is beyond the qualities"],["एते त्रयो गुणाः बध्नन्ति","these three qualities bind"],["तेन एव स्वातन्त्र्येण","by his own independence"],["स्थिति-आदि-अर्थम्","for maintenance and the other purposes"],["मायया गृहीताः","they are assumed through māyā"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":19,"end":19,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["वस्तुतः सर्वदा मुक्तम् अपि","although in reality always liberated"],["मायिनं माया-विषयं पुरुषम्","the living person subject to māyā"],["कार्यं अधिभूतम्","the effect is the अधिभूत"],["कारणम् अध्यात्मम्","the cause is the अध्यात्म"],["कर्ता अधिदैवतम्","the agent is the अधिदैवतम्"],["तेषां भावः तत्त्वम्","the nature, the reality of these"],["द्रव्यं महा-भूतानि","substance means the great elements"],["ज्ञान-शब्देन देवताः","the deities are referred to by the word ‘knowledge’"],["क्रिया इन्द्रियाणि","action means the senses"],["तद्-आश्रयाः कारण-भूताः","their supports are the causes"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":20,"end":20,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["स एष वश्यमायः","this very one, whose māyā is under control"],["एभिर् गुणैः","by these qualities"],["लिङ्गैर् जीवानाम् आवरकैः उपाधिभिः","by the marks and adjuncts that cover the living beings"],["सुष्ठु अलक्षिता गतिः","whose truth is very difficult to perceive"],["स्वैर् भक्तैः एव लक्षिता","perceived only by his own devotees"]],"note":"The source splits “सुष्ठ्व्-अलक्षिता” across its line; the WFW separates the compound and records that typographic break."},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":21,"end":21,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तस्य सृष्टि-प्रकारम्","the manner of his creation"],["कर्म जीवादृष्टम्","karma is the unseen result of the living being's acts"],["विबुभूषुः","desiring to become manifold"],["विविधं भवितुम् इच्छन्","wishing to be many"],["कालम् क्षोभकम्","time, the agitator"],["स्वभावम् परिणाम-हेतुम्","nature, the cause of transformation"],["सृष्ट्य्-अर्थम् अङ्गीकृतवान्","he accepted for the purpose of creation"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["गुणानां व्यतिकरः","the disturbance of the qualities"],["क्षोभः साम्य-त्यागः","agitation means the loss of equilibrium"],["स्वभावतः परिणामः","transformation through inherent nature"],["रूपान्तर-आपत्तिः","the assumption of another form"],["पुरुषः ईश्वरः","the Person is the Lord"],["तेन अधिष्ठितत्वम्","being governed by him"],["त्रयाणाम् विशेषणम्","an attribute of the three"],["महतः महत्-तत्त्वस्य","of the great principle, mahat"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["महत्-तत्त्वाद् विकुर्वाणात्","from the mahat principle as it transforms"],["क्रिया-ज्ञान-शक्तित्वात्","because it has the powers of action and knowledge"],["त्रिगुणत्वेऽपि","although it consists of three qualities"],["रजः-सत्त्वाभ्याम् उपबृंहितत्वम्","its being supported by rajas and sattva"],["अहंकारस्य आवरकत्वात्","because ahaṅkāra covers"],["तमः-प्रधानत्वम्","predominance of tamas"],["आकाशादिकम् बहु","ether and the rest are abundant"],["राजसं सात्त्विकं च अल्पम्","rajas and sattva are comparatively few"],["जीवेषु अपि तमसाधिक्यम्","likewise, tamas predominates in living beings"]],"note":"The source breaks “तमः-प्रधानत्वम्” across spaces; the WFW joins it as a single compound and records the source spacing defect."},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["स च विकुर्वन्","and it, transforming"],["रूपान्तरं गच्छन्","assuming another form"],["त्रैविध्यम् आह","he explains the threefold division"],["वैकारिकः सात्त्विकः","vaikārika means sāttvika"],["तैजसः राजसः","taijasa means rājasa"],["यद्-भिदा यस्य भेदः","the distinction by which it is divided"],["द्रव्य-शक्तिः","the power in substance"],["क्रिया-शक्तिः","the power in action"],["ज्ञान-शक्तिः","the power in knowledge"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["भूतादेः","of the elements and the rest"],["तामसस्य विशेषणम्","an attribute of the tāmasa principle"],["शब्दः नभसः मात्रा","sound is the subtle element of ether"],["सूक्ष्मं रूपम्","its subtle form"],["गुणः असाधारणः व्यावर्तकः धर्मः","a quality is a unique, distinguishing property"],["शब्द-द्वारा नभः उत्पद्यते","ether arises through sound"],["स्पर्शादिषु","in touch and the other elements"],["शब्दस्य लक्षणं लिङ्गम्","sound is a sign of its characteristic"],["लिङ्ग-विशेषणत्वात्","because it qualifies the sign"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":26,"end":26,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["परस्य नभसः कारणत्वेन अन्वयात्","because of its relation to ether as its cause"],["शब्दवान् च वायुः","air also possesses sound"],["तस्य लक्षणम्","its characteristic"],["प्राणः देह-धारणम्","prāṇa is the sustaining of the body"],["ओजः-सहः-बलानि","ojas, endurance and strength"],["इन्द्रिय-मनः-शरीराणां पाटवानि","the capacities of the senses, mind and body"],["तेषां हेतुः","the cause of those"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":27,"end":27,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["उदपद्यत उत्पन्नम्","arose, came into being"],["स्वतः रूपवत् तेजः","fire has form in itself"],["वायु-नभसोः कारण-भूतयोः अन्वयात्","because it inherits from air and ether, which are its causes"],["स्पर्श-शब्दवत् च","and it possesses touch and sound"],["अम्भसः पृथिव्याः च","of water and earth"],["पर-अन्वय-अधिक्यात्","because each further inherits more qualities"],["गुण-अधिक्यम्","there is an increase in qualities"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":28,"end":28,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["घोषः शब्दः","sound means a loud noise"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":29,"end":29,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["विशेषः पृथ्वी","the particular element is earth"],["पृथिव्याः च","and of earth"],["पर-अन्वय-अधिक्यात्","because of the greater inheritance from prior elements"],["गुण-अधिक्यम्","there is an increase in qualities"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":30,"end":30,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["मनः-शब्देन","by the word ‘mind’"],["तद्-अधिष्ठाता चन्द्रः","the moon, its presiding deity"],["दश देवाः वैकारिकाः","the ten deities are vaikārika"],["सात्त्विक-अहंकार-कार्याः","products of sāttvika ahaṅkāra"],["दिशः वातः अर्कः प्रचेताः अश्विनौ","the deities of directions, wind, sun, water and the Aśvins"],["श्रोत्र-त्वक्-चक्षुर्-जिह्वा-घ्राणानाम् अधिष्ठातारः","presiding over ear, skin, eye, tongue and nose"],["वह्निः इन्द्रः उपेन्द्रः मित्रः कः प्रजापतिः","fire, Indra, Upendra, Mitra, Yama and Prajāpati"],["वाक्-पाणि-पाद-पायूपस्थानाम् अधिष्ठातारः","presiding over speech, hands, feet, anus and genitals"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":31,"end":31,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["ज्ञान-शक्तिः बुद्धिः","the power of knowledge is the intellect"],["क्रिया-शक्तिः प्राणः","the power of action is prāṇa"],["तैजस-अहंकार-कार्यौ","both are products of taijasa ahaṅkāra"],["ज्ञान-क्रिया-विशेष-रूपाणि इन्द्रियाणि","the senses, which are forms of specialized knowledge and action"],["तैजसात् अभवन्","arose from the taijasa principle"],["श्रोत्रम्","the ear"],["दोः पाणिः","the arm is the hand"],["मेढ्रम् उपस्थः","the organ of generation is the genital"]],"note":"The source's final phrase “क्रमस् त्व् अत्र न विवक्षितह्” has a damaged ending; it is omitted from the gloss."},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":32,"end":32,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["कारण-सृष्टिम् उक्त्वा","having explained causal creation"],["कार्य-सृष्टिम् आह","he explains creation of the effects"],["एते असङ्गताः अमीलिताः","these were disconnected, unjoined"],["आयतनस्य शरीरस्य निर्माणे","in forming the body"],["न शेकुः","they were unable"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":33,"end":33,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["सद्-असत्त्वम्","the state of being principal or secondary"],["प्रधान-गुण-भावम्","the condition of having a principal quality"],["उपादाय स्वीकृत्य","having accepted"],["उभयं समष्टि-व्यष्ट्य्-आत्मकम् शरीरम्","the two bodies, cosmic and individual"],["ब्रह्माण्ड-अभिधम्","called the universe"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":34,"end":34,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["काल-कर्म-स्वभावान् अधिष्ठाय","presiding over time, karma and nature"],["स्थितः","situated"],["जीवयति इति जीवः","he causes life, therefore he is the living principle"],["परमात्मा","the Supreme Self"],["अजीवम् अचेतनम्","the nonliving, unconscious [principle]"],["अजीवयत् चेतयति स्म","he caused it to live, he made it conscious"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":35,"end":35,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["निर्भिद्य","having broken through"],["पृथक् कृत्य","having separated"],["स्थितः इति अर्थः","the meaning is that he remained apart"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":36,"end":36,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["तद्-अवयवैः","by its limbs"],["लोक-रचनाम्","the arrangement of the worlds"],["कटिः","the waist"],["ऊरु-मूलयोः पश्चाद्-भागः","the rear part at the roots of the thighs"],["जघनम् पुरो-भागः","the front of the lower body"],["अधः सप्त-लोकान् अतलादीन्","below are seven worlds, beginning with Atala"],["ऊर्ध्वं भूर्-आदीन् सप्त","above are seven, beginning with Bhūḥ"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":37,"end":37,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["वर्णानाम् ततः उत्पत्तिम्","the subsequent origin of the social classes"],["ब्रह्म ब्राह्मणः मुखम्","Brahman means the brāhmaṇa, the mouth"],["कार्य-कारणयोः अभेद-विवक्षया","with the intended non-difference of effect and cause"],["बाहवः इति च","and the arms"],["क्षत्रं क्षत्रियः","kṣatra means the kṣatriya"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":38,"end":38,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["उपासनार्थम्","for meditation"],["लोक-कल्पना-भेदान्","the different ways of conceiving the worlds"],["सप्त-लोक-पक्षम्","the view of seven worlds"],["भूर्-लोकः पातालम् आरभ्य","the Bhūrloka, beginning at Pātāla"],["पद्भ्यां कटि-पर्यन्ताभ्याम्","from the feet up to the waist"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":39,"end":39,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["स्तन-द्वयात् इति","with the words ‘from the two breasts’"],["उपासना-अर्थत्वात्","because this is for meditation"],["ऊर्ध्व-अधो-भाग-वैपरीत्यम् न दोषः","the reversal of above and below is not a fault"],["ब्रह्म-लोकः वैकुण्ठाख्यः","the world of Brahman, called Vaikuṇṭha"],["सनातनः नित्यः","eternal, permanent"],["न तु सृज्य-प्रपञ्च-अन्तर्-वर्ती","not within the created universe"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":40,"end":41,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["चतुर्दश-लोक-पक्षम्","the view of fourteen worlds"],["जघनादिभिः","by the lower body and the rest"],["भूर्-आदयः पूर्वोक्ताः एव सप्त","the seven worlds beginning with Bhūḥ, mentioned earlier"],["कट्य्-आदिभिः","by the waist and the other parts"],["अधः सप्त-लोकान्","the seven lower worlds"],["शुद्धम्","pure"],["हरि-भक्त-निवासत्वात्","because it is the dwelling place of Hari's devotees"]],"note":"The pinned Śrīdhara source groups 2.5.40–41 in one commentary block; the WFW range preserves that source grouping."},{"canto":2,"chapter":5,"start":42,"end":42,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/05_brahmANDanirmANavarNanam.md","source_blob_sha":"e93bbe709b6d47397953566b303f3b6ef04360de","pairs":[["त्रि-लोक-पक्षम्","the view of three worlds"],["भूर्-लोकः","the earthly world"],["पातालादि-सहितः","together with Pātāla and the rest"]]}]}